<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"> <channel><title>MiSTer FPGA Documentation</title><description>MiSTer FPGA is an open source project that aims to recreate various classic computers, game consoles, and arcade machines, using modern hardware.</description><link>https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/</link><atom:link href="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_updated.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml" /><managingEditor>Kevin Coleman</managingEditor><docs>https://github.com/HexFokker/MkDocs_MiSTer/</docs><language>en</language> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:17:22 -0000</pubDate> <lastBuildDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:17:22 -0000</lastBuildDate> <ttl>1440</ttl> <generator>MkDocs RSS plugin - v1.15.0</generator> <image> <url>assets/mister_kun_bw.svg</url> <title>MiSTer FPGA Documentation</title><link>https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/</link> </image> <item> <title>Home</title> <description>&lt;figure markdown&gt; ![MiSTer-kun Cat by hewhoisred and MiSTer Logo by Conrad Fenech](assets/logo_small.png){ align=center width=&#34;750&#34; } &lt;figcaption&gt;MiSTer-...</description><link>https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:24:11 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_updated.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/</guid> <enclosure url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/index.png" type="image/png" length="42205" /> </item> <item> <title>Editing These Docs</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;This guide shows how to edit this documentation site. It&#39;s similar to editing a wiki page, with a few extra steps. All edits are approved by the administrato...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/editing/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:24:11 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_updated.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/editing/</guid> <enclosure url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/editing.png" type="image/png" length="50394" /> </item> <item> <title>Audio Filters</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;The MiSTer has audio filters that make the audio sound less harsh and more balanced. Some old game systems were not designed for raw digital output: they had...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/audio/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:24:11 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_updated.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/audio/</guid> <enclosure url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/advanced/audio.png" type="image/png" length="47185" /> </item> <item> <title>Computer Core Networking</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Computer core Internet and console connections&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Since the May 7, 2018 release, MiSTer supports a serial (UART) connection from FPGA to Linux. Linux runs a ...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/computer/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:24:11 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_updated.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/computer/</guid> <enclosure url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/advanced/computer.png" type="image/png" length="56224" /> </item> <item> <title>Console Connection</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;The DE10-Nano board has a console port. It lets you log in to Linux without a network connection and provides debug/info output that is sometimes useful for ...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/console/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:24:11 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_updated.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/console/</guid> <enclosure url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/advanced/console.png" type="image/png" length="48318" /> </item> <item> <title>Using Your CRT With MiSTer</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;A few methods connect your MiSTer to a classic CRT display; the two main ones are the VGA port on the Analog I/O board and a Direct Video HDMI-to-VGA adapter...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/crt/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:24:11 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_updated.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/crt/</guid> <enclosure url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/advanced/crt.png" type="image/png" length="59029" /> </item> <item> <title>CRT Configuration Table</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;This table shows the &lt;code&gt;MiSTer.ini&lt;/code&gt; settings required for each analog video output mode when connecting to a CRT.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;CRT Configuration Table&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;| Analog Video O...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/crttable/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:24:11 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_updated.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/crttable/</guid> <enclosure url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/advanced/crttable.png" type="image/png" length="52950" /> </item> <item> <title>Direct Video Adapter</title> <description>&lt;h2&gt;Direct Video&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Since autumn 2019, &lt;em&gt;Direct Video&lt;/em&gt; has provided analog video output without an I/O board. It offers the &lt;strong&gt;same&lt;/strong&gt; minimal latency as the I/O bo...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/directvideo/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:24:11 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_updated.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/directvideo/</guid> <enclosure url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/advanced/directvideo.png" type="image/png" length="52046" /> </item> <item> <title>DIY 2-Player Arcade</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;by Sorgelig&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Assembled an arcade cabinet and looking to connect your joysticks and buttons? You don&#39;t need an expensive adapter — all you need is a USB key...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/diy2parcade/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:24:11 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_updated.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/diy2parcade/</guid> <enclosure url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/advanced/diy2parcade.png" type="image/png" length="51813" /> </item> <item> <title>INI Settings</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Main_MiSTer/blob/master/MiSTer.ini&#34;&gt;MiSTer.ini configuration file&lt;/a&gt;{target=_blank} contains global settings, and can also...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/ini/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:24:11 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_updated.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/ini/</guid> <enclosure url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/advanced/ini.png" type="image/png" length="47531" /> </item> <item> <title>Lag Explained</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;A common concern among retro enthusiasts is whether a device like MiSTer has &lt;em&gt;lag&lt;/em&gt; and whether it creates a less desirable experience than original hardware....&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/lag/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:24:11 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_updated.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/lag/</guid> <enclosure url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/advanced/lag.png" type="image/png" length="47531" /> </item> <item> <title>MGL Files</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;MGL files are shortcuts that load a game directly from the MiSTer Menu core. They can be placed in the root of the SD card to appear at the top of the menu, ...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/mgl/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:24:11 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_updated.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/mgl/</guid> <enclosure url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/advanced/mgl.png" type="image/png" length="45263" /> </item> <item> <title>MIDI Features</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;There are multiple options for using MIDI on the MiSTer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/dwhinham/mt32-pi/wiki&#34;&gt;The mt32-pi Project&lt;/a&gt;{target=_blank}&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Dale Whinham (a...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/midi/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:24:11 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_updated.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/midi/</guid> <enclosure url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/advanced/midi.png" type="image/png" length="46856" /> </item> <item> <title>Multi-Button Mapping</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;When you override the gamepad settings inside a core, you can also map button combinations (e.g. A+B) to a single button, if your gamepad has enough physical...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/multibutton/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:24:11 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_updated.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/multibutton/</guid> <enclosure url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/advanced/multibutton.png" type="image/png" length="51557" /> </item> <item> <title>Core Default Resolutions</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;This chart shows each core&#39;s default native resolution, frequencies, and pixel clock at startup. These values are not static and are documented for reference...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/nativeres/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:24:11 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_updated.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/nativeres/</guid> <enclosure url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/advanced/nativeres.png" type="image/png" length="55176" /> </item> <item> <title>Advanced Networking</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;The MiSTer has several advanced networking features.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Network access&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The MiSTer board can be accessed through the on-board Ethernet port. The system has *...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/network/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:24:11 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_updated.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/network/</guid> <enclosure url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/advanced/network.png" type="image/png" length="56033" /> </item> <item> <title>RTC Board</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;MiSTer FPGA RTC Add-on board&#34; src=&#34;img/rtc1.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Some cores (ao486, Minimig) use a clock, so MiSTer provides them with the real time. When an Internet connecti...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/rtc/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:24:11 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_updated.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/rtc/</guid> <enclosure url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/advanced/rtc.png" type="image/png" length="46717" /> </item> <item> <title>Video Modes</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;#!ini video_mode&lt;/code&gt; INI setting supports several ways to specify the video mode.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Automatic Detection&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;If no &lt;code&gt;#!ini video_mode&lt;/code&gt; setting is specified, Mi...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/videomodes/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:24:11 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_updated.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/videomodes/</guid> <enclosure url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/advanced/videomodes.png" type="image/png" length="47901" /> </item> <item> <title>Video Scaling</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;MiSTer has a built-in scaler that converts the cores&#39; low-resolution video to a higher resolution, optionally using filters to improve the picture on modern ...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/videoscaling/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:24:11 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_updated.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/videoscaling/</guid> <enclosure url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/advanced/videoscaling.png" type="image/png" length="51275" /> </item> <item> <title>Addon Boards</title> <description>&lt;figure markdown&gt; ![MiSTer FPGA Sandwich Punk Style Art by hewhoisred](img/misterpunk.png){ align=center width=&#34;400&#34; } &lt;figcaption&gt;Artwork by Hewhoisred&lt;...</description><link>https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/basics/addons/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:24:11 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_updated.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/basics/addons/</guid> <enclosure url="https://hexfokker.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/basics/addons.png" type="image/png" length="47930" /> </item> </channel></rss>